    "summary": "Built the pure \u00a74 rubbing ledger. Content (packages/content/src/objectives): the four types in a fixed order, stable ids <type>-<copy> (slice 2 types x 4 = 8, alpha 4 x 3 = 12), objectiveRules in 20 Hz ticks (collect/claim 120, choice 100, repeat-win 3600, seat 1200, gold 50, PvP 20% capped at 50), pvpGoldTransfer, and zod schemas/validators for source sites and the source assignment. Simulation (packages/simulation/src/objectives): LedgerState, where each rubbing has exactly one location (source/player/cache/duel reservation) plus a revision; seeded assignSources/createLedger; the operations addPlayer, unlockSource, startCollect, startCacheClaim, progressChannel, cancelChannel, reserveDuel, reportDuelResult, chooseTheft, advanceLedger (default theft at the deadline), disconnectPlayer, reconnectPlayer, expireReservation and quitPlayer. Each is (state, request) -> {state, result}; a rejected request returns the identical state object. checkLedger/assertLedger check the invariant. Added one ./objectives subpath export to each package.json, and docs/objectives.md. Tests: 28 scenario tests and 10 content tests, plus a property test (3 seeds x 2 presets, about 2700-5100 operations per sequence). Every operation runs on a deep-frozen state and is followed by an invariant check. Each seed is replayed to the same hashState, and coverage assertions prove each rule actually happened. A manual mutation check (4 injected bugs) made the tests fail each time. Checks executed in the worktree after npm ci: npm run typecheck (exit 0), npm run test:unit (317/317; an earlier run had 1 timeout in the existing maps.test.ts at host load 12.5, after which I shrank my property test from ~11 s to ~4 s and the rerun passed), npm run test:integration (22/22), npm run build (exit 0, smoke passed). Also checked by hand that both new subpaths resolve to and load from dist/, and that tests/unit/purity.test.ts flags a Math.random planted in each new directory (planted files removed). Nothing committed.",
